{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.weightedCharacterTrace_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.weightedCharacterTrace_nil","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L228-L242","doc":"**The weighted trace at the identity is the `y`-weighted dimension sum.**\n`tr_M(1) = Σ_λ y_λ · d_λ`, since each block character at the empty word is\nthe block dimension (`χ^λ(1) = tr(𝟙_{d_λ}) = d_λ`).  Hence the Markov\nnormalisation (M1) `tr_M(1) = 1` is exactly the weight condition\n`Σ_λ y_λ · d_λ = 1` — the relation that pins the `y_λ` once the block\ndimensions are known.  Bean `qou-xq3f` (T2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.weightedCharacterTrace_append_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.weightedCharacterTrace_append_comm","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L213-L226","doc":"**The Wedderburn-weighted trace inherits Markov cyclicity (M2).**  Each\nblock character is a class function (`character_append_comm`), so any\n`y`-weighted sum of them is one too:\n`tr_M(v ++ w) = tr_M(w ++ v)`.  Independent of the particular `y_λ`; the\nstructural prerequisite for `tr_M = Σ_λ y_λ χ^λ` being a genuine Markov\ntrace.  Bean `qou-xq3f` (T2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.weightedCharacterTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.weightedCharacterTrace","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L205-L211","doc":"The **Wedderburn-weighted Markov trace**: `Σ_{i ∈ s} y i · χ^{(i)}(w)`, a\n`y`-weighted sum of per-block characters over a finite index set `s`, each\nblock `i` carrying its own dimension `dim i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.character_conj_word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.character_conj_word","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L168-L186","doc":"**Generator-conjugation invariance of the Markov trace on braid words.**\nPrepending `σ_i` and appending `σ_i⁻¹` to a word `w` leaves the\nrepresentation character unchanged:\n`tr_ρ((i,+) :: (w ++ [(i,−)])) = tr_ρ(w)`.\n\nThis is the word-level statement of `trace_conj_gen`, obtained by\nevaluating the singleton generators via `eval_append`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.trace_conj_genInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.trace_conj_genInv","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L161-L166","doc":"**Conjugation by a generator inverse `σ_i⁻¹` preserves the trace**:\n`tr(σ_i⁻¹ · A · σ_i) = tr(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.trace_conj_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.trace_conj_gen","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L154-L159","doc":"**Conjugation by a generator `σ_i` preserves the trace** at the matrix\nlevel: `tr(σ_i · A · σ_i⁻¹) = tr(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_append_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_append_comm","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L140-L143","doc":"`markovTrace` form of `character_append_comm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.character_append_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.character_append_comm","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L128-L138","doc":"**Cyclic invariance of the Markov trace** (the `tr(ab) = tr(ba)` property\nat the level of braid words): the character is unchanged under cyclic\nrotation of the word,\n`tr_ρ(v ++ w) = tr_ρ(w ++ v)`.\n\nThis is the *class-function* property — the character depends only on the\nconjugacy class of the braid, not the specific word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.trace_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.trace_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L123-L126","doc":"**Trace property `tr(AB) = tr(BA)`** at the matrix level, on the\nrepresentation ground ring.  Restatement of `Matrix.trace_mul_comm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_eq_character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_eq_character","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L120-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.markovTrace","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L113-L118","doc":"The **Markov trace of a braid word** on a representation `ρ`: the matrix\ntrace of the evaluated word.  Definitionally equal to\n`HeckeRep.character ρ w`; named here to make the trace-functional role\nexplicit.  Maps `H_n(q) → R_t` (through the chosen representation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.trace_conj_of_mul_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTrace.trace_conj_of_mul_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L94-L107","doc":"**Trace of a two-sided conjugate.**  If `N · M = 1` then\n`tr(M · A · N) = tr(A)` for any square matrix `A`.\n\nWith `N = M⁻¹` this is the usual similarity-invariance\n`tr(M A M⁻¹) = tr(A)`; stated with a bare left-inverse hypothesis so it\napplies to the Hecke generator/inverse pair, which are two-sided inverses\nof each other but only a *one*-sided hypothesis is needed here.\n\nTODO upstream: `Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace` — companion to\n`Matrix.trace_mul_comm` / `Matrix.trace_mul_cycle`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.eval_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.eval_append","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovTrace.lean#L67-L80","doc":"**Evaluation is a monoid homomorphism.**  Evaluating the concatenation\nof two braid words is the product of their evaluations:\n`ρ.eval (v ++ w) = ρ.eval v * ρ.eval w`.\n\nThis is the structural fact that makes `HeckeRep.character` behave like a\ntrace on the braid monoid.  Proved by induction on the first word. ","signatureChunk":0}]}